Z||000004||DRH||01-18-2001||11:34 PM||||The easiest, and probably most cost effective way, would be to sell yours and buy a 5 speed (or trade zeus  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )<P>If you still want to do it, you could probably get everything used as long as it's in good shape. I'd probably go new on the clutch, pressure plate and throwout bearing unless you run across good as new stuff though.<P>Buying a non-runner cheap might be your best bet so you can have anything you're missing readily available. Plus you can see how it came apart.<P>Off the top of my head:<BR>tranny (with shifter and slave brackets)<BR>flywheel<BR>clutch, pressure plate, throw out bearing<BR>axles<BR>shifter<BR>shifter cables<BR>clutch master cyl<BR>clutch slave cyl<BR>clutch line<BR>ECM (or at least the chip, programming is different)<BR>clutch/brake pedal assembly (the whole thing)<BR>clutch switch<P>Some wiring differences for: starter interlock (clutch vs. park/neutral), trunk release, reverse lights, shift light vs torque convertor solenoid. Look over a wiring diagram.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||pHoOl||01-19-2001||02:29 AM||||Yeah zeus, what do you have? <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
